The graph of $y=f(x)$ is a concave up parabola with vertex at $(1,-1)$.

Horizontal transformations:

(1) reflection in the $y$-axis;

(2) translation to the right by 1 unit.

Vertical transformations:

(1) dilation by factor 2;

(2) translation down by 6 units.

$x$-coordinate of transformed vertex: $1\times(-1)+1=0$.

$y$-coordinate of transformed vertex: $(-1)\times 2-6=-8$.

\exfigure{1346_q26_sol_1}

\exfigure{1365_q21_s1}

The total area under the curve is $1$ and the area between $-N$ and $N$ is $p$, so the two tails together have area $1-p$. By symmetry each tail has area $\dfrac{1-p}{2}$.
$$\begin{aligned} P(z<N) &= 1-\dfrac{1-p}{2} \\ &= \dfrac12+\dfrac{p}{2} \end{aligned}$$

