The diagram below shows the graph of $y=f'(x)$.

\exfigure{1290_q28_1}

Sketch a possible graph of $y=f(x)$ below, including axes and any stationary points.

items.sol:
At a stationary point $f'(x)=0$, so there are stationary points at $x=-4$ and $x=2$.

$$\begin{aligned} f'(x) &> 0 &&\text{for } x<-4 &&\text{increasing}\\ f'(x) &< 0 &&\text{for } -4<x<2 &&\text{decreasing}\\ f'(x) &> 0 &&\text{for } x>2 &&\text{increasing} \end{aligned}$$Hence there is a maximum at $x=-4$ and a minimum at $x=2$.

