items.sol:
\exfigure{631_q7c_s1}

The curve is above the line on $\left[0, \dfrac{\pi}{3}\right]$, so the area is

$$\begin{aligned} \text{Area} &= \int_0^{\frac{\pi}{3}} \left(\cos x - \dfrac{1}{2}\right)dx \\ &= \left[\sin x - \dfrac{x}{2}\right]_0^{\frac{\pi}{3}} \\ &= \left(\sin\dfrac{\pi}{3} - \dfrac{\pi}{6}\right) - \left(\sin 0 - 0\right) \\ &= \dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2} - \dfrac{\pi}{6} \\ &= \dfrac{3\sqrt{3} - \pi}{6} \text{ units}^2 \end{aligned}$$

